WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.134
Apple Silicon systems combine CPU cores, GPU cores, unified memory, storage,

00:00:04.134 --> 00:00:06.701
and specialized accelerators inside an integrated platform.

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:08.901
Performance cores handle demanding CPU work,

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:12.568
while efficiency cores help with lighter tasks and power management.

00:00:12.568 --> 00:00:16.969
GPU cores can accelerate supported local inference workflows through runtimes that use

00:00:16.969 --> 00:00:18.803
Apple's graphics and compute stack.

00:00:18.803 --> 00:00:22.470
Storage speed affects model loading, dataset handling, and general responsiveness.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:26.504
The Neural Engine is important in Apple's broader machine learning ecosystem,

00:00:26.504 --> 00:00:30.904
but local LLM runtimes do not automatically use it for every workload.

00:00:30.904 --> 00:00:36.039
Many local language model workflows rely more heavily on CPU and GPU execution paths,

00:00:36.039 --> 00:00:37.505
especially through Metal-enabled runtimes.

00:00:37.505 --> 00:00:40.806
It is useful to know the Neural Engine exists,

00:00:40.806 --> 00:00:45.573
but it should not be assumed to solve every local inference performance problem.

00:00:45.573 --> 00:00:48.874
Unified memory is one of the biggest planning factors.

00:00:48.874 --> 00:00:53.641
A Mac with more memory can often run larger models, larger context windows,

00:00:53.641 --> 00:00:56.575
or more simultaneous services than a lower-memory system.

00:00:56.575 --> 00:01:00.976
But total memory is shared by macOS, applications, model weights, runtime overhead,

00:01:00.976 --> 00:01:03.543
context buffers, browser tabs, and background services.

00:01:03.543 --> 00:01:08.310
Available memory for inference is always less than the headline system memory number.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:11.977
Thermal design, battery, and power behavior matter for sustained workloads.

00:01:11.977 --> 00:01:16.378
A MacBook may run a short test quickly but reduce performance during

00:01:16.378 --> 00:01:18.211
long generation or batch work.

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:21.145
A desktop Mac may sustain load more comfortably.

00:01:21.145 --> 00:01:25.912
When planning an Apple Silicon LLM setup, think about memory capacity, memory bandwidth,

00:01:25.912 --> 00:01:31.047
cooling, storage space, and whether the machine will be used interactively, as a service,

00:01:31.047 --> 00:01:31.780
or both.
